{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ndcxaha4favrakce5bo5u7c4op3356r4uho6tnr6yccfgefovhua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — **the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte on every path tested. No divergences found; no fixes were needed.**\n\n## What the library is\nA single C translation unit (`c_src/src/driver.c`, 66 lines) exporting 5 symbols: `printLine`, `printIntLine`, `bad`, `good`, `driver`. All 5 were already translated in `translation/src/lib.rs` — no missing modules, nothing to translate.\n\n## Artifacts (crate root)\n| File | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` inventory, 5/5 exported, symbol diff **empty**, 0 undefined non-libc symbols |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 10 rows — derived from the *only* rejection in the C (`if (line != NULL)`; no `return`, no `assert`, no error enum) plus mandatory generic boundaries |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 18 rows — all 5 entry points incl. the low-level leaves, cross-producted with input shapes |\n\n## Tests (`translation/tests/`, 32 total, all passing)\n- `common/mod.rs` — loads **both** `.so`s via `libloading`, calls only exported symbols, captures stdout per call via `dup2` on fd 1 (file-backed, so 256 KiB outputs don't deadlock), seeded SplitMix64 RNG.\n- `phase_b_configs.rs` — 18 tests, one per `CONFIGS.md` row (~3 000 randomized cases: all 255 single-byte values, random non-UTF-8 buffers, lengths up to 65 537, full-range `i32`, 8 randomized 256-step interleaved programs across all 5 entry points).\n- `phase_c_errors.rs` — 10 tests, one per `ERRORS.md` row.\n- `phase_d_symbols.rs` — enforces the empty symbol diff as a test.\n- `scripts/verify_all.sh` — sweeps profiles × feature combos; the crate declares no `[features]`, so it runs default and `--no-default-features` in debug + release (4 configs, all pass). A test pins the \"no features\" assumption so the sweep must be extended if that changes.\n\n## Notable behaviors deliberately preserved\n- **`bad()` prints `0\\n0\\n`** — the CWE-482 discarded-expression defect. Not \"fixed.\"\n- **`printLine(NULL)` prints nothing at all** — not even a newline.\n- **Non-UTF-8 bytes pass through verbatim.** GCC lowers `printf(\"%s\\n\", s)` to `puts(s)`; the Rust keeps raw `*const c_char` + `printf`, so arbitrary bytes are byte-identical.\n\n## Harness sensitivity proven\nRather than trust green tests, I built two deliberately broken Rust `.so`s and confirmed the suite catches them:\n- \"fixing\" `bad()` to print `0\\n2\\n` → 7 tests fail with explicit `DIVERGENCE` reports\n- routing `printLine` through `String::from_utf8_lossy` → 7 tests fail (incl. `C2`, `C4`, `E4`)\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: `[profile.release] panic = \"abort\"` applies to test binaries too, so a release-mode divergence aborts the process instead of listing failures. Debug mode gives readable reports; `verify_all.sh` runs both.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":834,"cache_read_input_tokens":65161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":834,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f808d1ae-9bc1-4ec4-acd4-9917e538a912","uuid":"fe009e6f-6262-45a7-b816-6a9ca55c9854","timestamp":"2026-09-05T03:33:04.557Z"}
